[{:db/id 17592186287725 :question/problem "![](images/32/32168a2cb1fe14dbc88725347611ae5951198e81dfaa0b41e780106750bbb741.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,3x\\,{{field-2}}\\,y\\,{{field-3}}\\,\\frac{x}{4}\\}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points in our set include all those that lie *above* the line $y=3x$ and *below* the line $y=\\frac{x}{4}.$\n\nA point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>3x,\\,y<\\frac{x}{4}.\n$$\n\nCombining this into a single condition, we have\n\n$$\n3x<y<\\frac{x}{4}.\n$$\n\nWe must also include the line $y=3x$ since the boundary is included in the set (the curve is solid). So, we change the corresponding inequality symbol above as follows:\n\n$$\n3x\\le y<\\frac{x}{4}\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,3x\\le y<\\frac{x}{4}\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186287768 :question/problem "![](images/66/664c70223ca8a6219b04a287c779d20bf0f88d770920d1357303721574d90787.png)\n\nUse set builder notation to describe the shaded region given in the diagram above:\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,y\\,{{field-2}}\\,{x}^{2}\\}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points in our set include all those that lie *above* the curve $y={x}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, a point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following condition is satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>{x}^{2}\n$$\n\nWe must also include the curve $y={x}^{2}$ since the boundary is included in the set (the curve is solid). So, we change the inequality symbol above as follows:\n\n$$\ny\\ge {x}^{2}\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\ge {x}^{2}\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186287798 :question/problem "![](images/98/980ae73286ed41ed0c6f074a4bed5b35fa852dd608fb0a1a561f26a7eac60ea7.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,x\\,{{field-2}}\\,2\\}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since all points $P(x,y)$ in our set lie at integer values of $x$ and $y,$ we have $x\\in Z,y\\in Z,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in Z\\times Z={Z}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe points in our set include all those that lie *to the left* the line $x=2.$ For those points, the following condition is satisfied:\n\n$$\nx<2\n$$\n\nSince the boundary is *not* included in the set (the curve is *not* solid),  no further action must be taken, so we have\n\n$$\nx<2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {Z}^{2}\\,:\\,x<2\\}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-ec96477c-3148-5d64-92ac-70e802659d96" :activity/id #uuid "ec96477c-3148-5d64-92ac-70e802659d96" :activity/title "Describing Planar Regions Using Set-Builder Notation" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186051063 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-d944585f-3405-5ba6-8dae-d59dced3f322" "step-d4b86ca5-af6d-53a9-a974-2a88b2674a7b" "step-2c3e1240-c726-51bb-964e-3c47808e7b7e" "step-5b59b1f7-7c69-53e1-bf66-88abd240720f" "step-2c9136d1-b775-59b9-8793-3bb26263467c"] :activity/first-step "step-d944585f-3405-5ba6-8dae-d59dced3f322" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-d944585f-3405-5ba6-8dae-d59dced3f322" :step/id #uuid "d944585f-3405-5ba6-8dae-d59dced3f322" :step/content 17592186198790 :step/next "step-d4b86ca5-af6d-53a9-a974-2a88b2674a7b" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-d4b86ca5-af6d-53a9-a974-2a88b2674a7b" :step/id #uuid "d4b86ca5-af6d-53a9-a974-2a88b2674a7b" :step/content 17592186287725 :step/next "step-2c3e1240-c726-51bb-964e-3c47808e7b7e" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-2c3e1240-c726-51bb-964e-3c47808e7b7e" :step/id #uuid "2c3e1240-c726-51bb-964e-3c47808e7b7e" :step/content 17592186287768 :step/next "step-5b59b1f7-7c69-53e1-bf66-88abd240720f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-5b59b1f7-7c69-53e1-bf66-88abd240720f" :step/id #uuid "5b59b1f7-7c69-53e1-bf66-88abd240720f" :step/content 17592186287790 :step/next "step-2c9136d1-b775-59b9-8793-3bb26263467c" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-2c9136d1-b775-59b9-8793-3bb26263467c" :step/id #uuid "2c9136d1-b775-59b9-8793-3bb26263467c" :step/content 17592186287798 :db/ensure [:step/validate]}]
